From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FerrionOS contributors <contributors@ferrion.invalid>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 14:33:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] backend: Add per-head zero-copy GBM swapchain presenter (Stage B1)

Create the GBM device once during backend init before WAYLAND_DISPLAY
is set (asserted at creation) and keep it for the compositor's lifetime
so Mesa's device-select layer cannot self-connect to ferrion-wm's
Wayland socket on reconfigure once Mesa's Wayland platform is enabled.
Open a per-head LINEAR GBM swapchain (SWAPCHAIN_SLOTS = 2 <=
MAX_DMABUF_FBS_PER_HEAD = 3, MAX_IN_FLIGHT_FLIPS = 1) only when
present_mode is PageFlip, the GlesRenderer EGLDisplay advertises a
LINEAR dma-buf render format, /scheme/gpu.* exists, gbm_create_device
succeeds, and every BO binds into GlesRenderer and registers with
DRM_IOCTL_MODE_ADDFB2. Any failure logs FERRION_PRESENTER with
swapchain=cpu and the failing step and stays on Stage A's CPU readback
path. If another display change arrives mid-setup, stay ChangePending
until the queued DisplayChanged reconfigures.

Track per-slot Free/InFlight/OnScreen state with assertions so only a
Free slot is rendered into and the OnScreen slot becomes Free only on
FlipComplete. Wait on result.sync before present_dmabuf_for, log
copy_us=0, and tear down every head's FBs, GEM handles, and BOs (while
keeping the GBM device) on ChangePending and reconfigure, dropping the
GBM device only when Ferrion drops.
